{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Multiset.Basic"],"declarations":45,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.mass_from_graded_content_cannot_separate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.mass_from_graded_content_cannot_separate","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L284-L292","doc":"**The `(n,T₃)` content alone cannot witness `breaks_graded_collision`.**\nAny mass map that is a *function of the graded content* assigns D̄⁰ and K⁰\nthe *same* mass — so it fails the conjecture's separation field.  This is\nthe precise sense in which `T₃` resolves the *selection* but not the\n*geometry*: the mass datum is provably not a function of `(n,T₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid.breaks_graded_collision","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid.breaks_graded_collision","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L282-L282","doc":"The geometry must separate the residual graded-content collision\nD̄⁰ ≡ K⁰: same `(n,T₃)` content, sharply different mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid.mass_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid.mass_positive","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L279-L279","doc":"The mass law reads the hyperbolic volume (volume–density mass form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid.hyperbolic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid.hyperbolic","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L277-L277","doc":"Every meson's canonical braid is genuinely hyperbolic (positive volume),\nnot the `Vol = 0` torus carrier the `(n,T₃)` content provides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid.mk","kind":"ctor","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L274-L274","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.CanonicalHyperbolicMesonBraid","kind":"class","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L251-L282","doc":"**Primary conjecture (open — deliberately NO instance).**\n\nRefining the operator-selection input to `(n, T₃)` fixes *which* meson\ncontent is selected (proved above), but **not** the hyperbolic braid word\nthat carries the mass.  The graded content is `Vol = 0` torus-carrier data\n(`MesonFluxTubeReduction.twoStrand_winding_bijective`); the mass needs a\ngenuinely *hyperbolic* braid at `H₃(q)` (Obstruction A, `qou-qpj9`).\n\nA canonical realization would provide volume/mass maps such that:\n\n* `hyperbolic` — every meson's canonical braid has *positive* volume (not\n  the `Vol = 0` carrier the `(n,T₃)` content alone gives);\n* `mass_positive` — the mass law reads off that volume;\n* `breaks_graded_collision` — the geometry supplies data *beyond*\n  `(n,T₃)`: though `gradedContent .Dmeson = gradedContent .K0`\n  (`graded_D_K0_collide`), the physical masses differ sharply\n  (`m_D ≈ 1865 ≫ m_K ≈ 498`), so the braid word must carry the residual\n  flavour datum the content lacks.\n\nContent-bearing (each field is a genuine constraint), and **no instance is\nprovided** — constructing the canonical hyperbolic meson braid from the\ngraded content is the open step `qou-qpj9`.  A fabricated instance over\nthis finite toy would be forbidden laundering (§3b-tax). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.orderedContent_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.orderedContent_injective","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L241-L247","doc":"**…but the ordered content IS injective.**  Keeping the quark/antiquark\norientation (the \"bar\" — itself topological strand-orientation data, not\na fit) separates D̄⁰ `(−5,+3)` from K⁰ `(+3,−5)`.  The residual collision\nis an artefact of the *symmetric-multiset* content model of #4614, not of\nthe physics; the bar resolves it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.gradedContentExt_not_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.gradedContentExt_not_injective","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L235-L239","doc":"Hence the signed content is **not** injective on the full meson set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.graded_D_K0_collide","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.graded_D_K0_collide","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L226-L233","doc":"**Residual collision.**  With the neutral kaon `K⁰ = d̄s` admitted, the\nsigned *multiset* still collides D̄⁰ `{−5,+3}` with K⁰ `{+3,−5}`: `(n,T₃)`\ngrades by *(generation, weak-sign)*, and `c̄` shares `(5, −)` with `s`,\n`u` shares `(3, +)` with `d̄`.  So `T₃` does not *globally* separate all\nmesons — a further flavour grading (charm number vs strangeness) is the\nremaining missing datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.gradedContent_injective_on_dictionary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.gradedContent_injective_on_dictionary","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L215-L222","doc":"**The refined selection is injective on the four-meson dictionary.**  On\n`{pion, kaon, etaPhi, Dmeson}` the signed content distinguishes every\nmeson — the operator-selection is no longer degenerate on the domain the\nblocker lived in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.graded_D_kaon_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.graded_D_kaon_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L208-L213","doc":"**THE RESULT.** The signed content **separates** D̄⁰ from the kaon: the\ncharm-antiquark `c̄` (`−κ = −5`) vs the up-antiquark `ū` (`−κ = −3`)\nbreaks the tie the magnitude hid.  The specific degeneracy the audit\nnamed is resolved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.unsignedContent_not_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.unsignedContent_not_injective","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L201-L206","doc":"**The unsigned selection is degenerate** (reproduces\n`winding_content_not_injective`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.unsigned_D_kaon_collide","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.unsigned_D_kaon_collide","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L196-L199","doc":"**The blocker.** The unsigned content collides D̄⁰ `{5,3}` with the kaon\n`{3,5}` — exactly `MesonFluxTubeReduction.D_kaon_same_winding`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.orderedContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.orderedContent","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L189-L192","doc":"**Ordered signed content** `(−κ(antiquark), +κ(quark))` — keeps the\nquark/antiquark orientation (the \"bar\") as ordered data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.gradedContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.gradedContent","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L183-L187","doc":"**Signed writhe content** `{−κ(antiquark), +κ(quark)}` — the *refined*\ninput.  The antiquark reverses the braid orientation, hence contributes\n`−κ` (topological, not fitted). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.unsignedContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.unsignedContent","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L177-L181","doc":"**Unsigned winding content** `{|κ₁|, |κ₂|}` — the input of\n`MesonFluxTubeReduction.windingContent` (a symmetric function of the two\ngenerations). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instDecidablePredMesonInDictionary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instDecidablePredMesonInDictionary","kind":"instance","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L174-L175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.inDictionary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.inDictionary","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L168-L172","doc":"Is this meson in the four-meson dictionary of `lepton-meson-torus-knot-\ndictionary` (i.e. not the extension `K⁰`)? ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.constituents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.constituents","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L160-L166","doc":"The `(antiquark, quark)` constituent pair of each meson. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instFintypeMeson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instFintypeMeson","kind":"instance","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L158-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instDecidableEqMeson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instDecidableEqMeson","kind":"instance","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L158-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.K0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.K0","kind":"ctor","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L157-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.Dmeson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.Dmeson","kind":"ctor","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L156-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.etaPhi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.etaPhi","kind":"ctor","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L155-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.kaon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.kaon","kind":"ctor","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L154-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.pion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson.pion","kind":"ctor","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L153-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Meson","kind":"inductive","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L149-L158","doc":"The four-meson dictionary of `lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary`, plus\nthe neutral kaon `K⁰ = d̄s` (used below to expose the residual collision).\nA meson is recorded as its `(antiquark, quark)` pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.T3_charm_ne_strange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.T3_charm_ne_strange","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L141-L145","doc":"Charm's `T₃` is `+½`, strange's is `−½` (the `ℚ`-level statement). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.charmBlock_ne_strangeBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.charmBlock_ne_strangeBlock","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L135-L139","doc":"**…but their selection inputs differ** — the sign (`+` vs `−`) breaks the\ntie: the charm block `(5, +1)` is distinctly selectable from the strange\nblock `(5, −1)`.  This is the datum the unsigned winding lacked. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.charm_strange_same_generation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.charm_strange_same_generation","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L130-L133","doc":"**Charm and strange share the generation winding** (both `n = 5`) — the\ndegeneracy `winding_content_not_injective` records. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.selectionInput_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.selectionInput_injective","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L125-L128","doc":"**The refined selection input is injective.**  `(n, 2T₃)` distinguishes\nevery quark, so each Wedderburn/knot block is individually selectable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.signedWrithe_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.signedWrithe_injective","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L119-L123","doc":"**`signedWrithe` separates all six quarks.**  The generation-plus-sign\ndatum is a complete label — the collision that made the unsigned winding\nnon-injective is gone at the quark level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.selectionInput","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.selectionInput","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L114-L117","doc":"**The refined operator-selection demand input** for a single quark: the\npair `(generation winding, weak sign) = (n, 2·T₃)`.  The unsigned input\nused by `winding_content_not_injective` is only its first coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.T3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.T3","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L109-L110","doc":"Weak isospin `T₃ = sign(κ)/2 ∈ {+½,−½}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.genWinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.genWinding","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L106-L107","doc":"Generation winding `n = |κ| ∈ {3,5,7}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.signedWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.signedWrithe","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L98-L104","doc":"The *signed* writhe `κ = ±n` of a quark's canonical `T(2,n) = σ₁^{±n}`\nbraid.  Magnitude `|κ| = n` is the generation winding (`u,d = 3`,\n`s,c = 5`, `b,t = 7`); the sign is the `⋈_K`-inherited orientation\n(up-type positive, down-type negative).  Mirrors PR #4618. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instFintypeQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instFintypeQuark","kind":"instance","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instDecidableEqQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.instDecidableEqQuark","kind":"instance","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.bottom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.bottom","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.strange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.strange","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.down","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.top","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.charm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.charm","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark.up","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonOperatorSelectionT3.Quark","kind":"inductive","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonOperatorSelectionT3.lean#L92-L96","doc":"The six SM quark flavours. ","signatureChunk":0}]}